# P0 credential-exposure containment (2026-11-09): .vercel-env-vars.txt was
# tracked since this repo's initial commit and contained real DATABASE_URL,
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID/SECRET, and NEXTAUTH_SECRET values -- untracked and
# removed in this same change. This pattern is intentionally broader than
# the one file removed, to also catch any future "copy these into the
# Vercel dashboard" helper file using the same naming convention. This does
# NOT cover the other, separately-tracked credential-bearing files found
# during the same investigation (env-list.txt, .env.neon,
# .env.production.protected-backup, gitkraken.env, the Google OAuth
# client_secret_*.json, several .env.local.backup.* files, and duplicates
# under _archive/) -- those remain tracked and require their own,
# separate containment decision; see
# VYAPARSETHU_P0_CREDENTIAL_EXPOSURE_CONTAINMENT_REPORT.md.
.vercel-env*.txt
